B.Xk=new A.aI(B.XV,[u.H,"FAIRY TALE GENRE RULES:\n- Placeholder \u2014 add your custom rules for fairy tale stories here.\n- Consider: types of magical creatures, settings, moral lessons, and story structures you prefer.","ANIMAL ADVENTURE GENRE RULES:\n\nHABITAT VARIETY (CRITICAL):\n- Every story must be set in a DIFFERENT habitat. Rotate through: ocean, coral reef, rainforest, savanna, arctic/antarctic, woodland, wetland/swamp, desert, mountain, freshwater river/lake.\n- Do NOT default to beach or tide pool repeatedly.\n- Choose the habitat randomly and commit to it fully.\n\nANIMAL VARIETY (CRITICAL):\n- Do NOT default to crabs, monkeys, dolphins, elephants, or lions.\n- Every story must feature at least ONE animal most children have never heard of.\n- Less common animals to consider: capybara, axolotl, pangolin, okapi, quokka, binturong, shoebill stork, narwhal, sun bear, kakapo, fossa, tardigrade, mantis shrimp, leafy sea dragon, star-nosed mole, and many others.\n- Familiar animals are fine as supporting characters but the STAR must be less common.\n\nANIMAL FACTS (REQUIRED):\n- Include at least ONE surprising true fact per turn about the featured animal.\n- Facts must be age-appropriate and genuinely surprising.\n- Weave facts naturally into the story \u2014 never as a lecture.\n\nSTORY ARC VARIETY:\n- Vary the story arc each time: animal finding food, raising young, seasonal migration, escaping a predator safely, finding shelter, animal friendships across species, recovering from injury with a ranger's help.\n\nREALISM:\n- Animals behave realistically \u2014 no talking animals unless genre is fairy tale.\n- Show real animal behaviors: hunting, nesting, communicating, playing.\n- Conservation themes welcome but keep them hopeful, not scary.","ATHLETIC ACHIEVEMENT GENRE RULES:\n- Placeholder \u2014 add your custom rules for athletic achievement stories here.\n- Consider: specific sports, teamwork themes, perseverance, and age-appropriate challenges.","FAVORITE VACATION GENRE RULES:\n- Placeholder \u2014 add your custom rules for vacation stories here.\n- Consider: types of destinations, travel adventures, cultural experiences, and family activities.","FRIENDSHIP GENRE RULES:\n- Placeholder \u2014 add your custom rules for friendship stories here.\n- Consider: conflict resolution, inclusion, kindness, and age-appropriate social situations.","SCHOOL DAY GENRE RULES:\n- Placeholder \u2014 add your custom rules for school day stories here.\n- Consider: subjects, teachers, classroom situations, learning moments, and social dynamics.","SPACE TRAVEL GENRE RULES:\n- Placeholder \u2014 add your custom rules for space travel stories here.\n- Consider: planets, space phenomena, alien life, spacecraft, and age-appropriate science facts.","TYPE YOUR OWN STORY RULES:\n- Placeholder \u2014 add your custom rules for open-ended stories here.\n- Consider: how much creative freedom to give, guardrails, and themes to encourage."],t.w)
